  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, concat fusion) achieves 0.527 acc, clearly above rna_only (0.485) and far above image_only (0.208), suggesting the multimodal direction is promising and that the image modality contributes complementary signal. However, we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat). Uncertainty: it is unknown whether the modest gain from adding image is sensitive to how the two modalities are combined; weighted fusion could better balance the strong RNA signal against the weaker image signal. This experiment (config_017) is a clean single-variable change from config_016—only fusion switches from concat to weighted—so any accuracy/F1 difference can be attributed to the fusion strategy. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information next step: it either confirms concat is sufficient (freeing us to explore profile/encoder/image-encoder changes) or reveals that weighted fusion is materially better, which would redirect all subsequent multimodal experiments. It avoids introducing multiple new variables (profile, aggregation, new encoders) simultaneously."
}

